vents","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"content_type":"application/json","state":"uploaded","size":653,"digest":"sha256:0109ccd673df95e6b24a11ccb6a959bcb39120916cd734c0cde889eccaaf1d59","download_count":0,"created_at":"2026-11-20T16:20:29Z","updated_at":"2026-11-20T16:20:30Z","browser_download_url":"https://github.com/enginsoysal/engacer-os/releases/download/m145-v0.14.5/m14stage5-starter-manifest.json"}],"tarball_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/enginsoysal/engacer-os/tarball/m145-v0.14.5","zipball_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/enginsoysal/engacer-os/zipball/m145-v0.14.5","body":"# Engacer OS M14.5 - Original menus, folders and controls\n\nNative qualification passes within **M14-STAGE5-VM-v1**. The matching tested media and current guides are linked below. Public download and website receipts record their separate delivery checks. Reported BrixCanvas search/navigation limitations remain explicitly nonblocking.\n\nM14.5 adds original 7-Zip x64 menus/About dialog, toolbar images, list details and Documents/subfolder/Backspace navigation preview through the own native compatibility APIs. Existing console/MSI tasks remain supported. Full GUI archive tasks, Notepad++/Sumatra interfaces and Firefox execution remain unqualified. All three original target scenarios remain mandatory in M14.12; whole-system CPU/RAM/storage optimization blocks final M14.15.\n\nBuild `06c8de63a527c32ad9ec73f4b9e333bc` binds **695 exact compiled inputs**. Original Windows program instructions and callbacks run in protected native processes through our own kernel; an embedded Windows guest or app imitation is not the implementation.\n\n- ISO SHA-256: `fdae44b21bc47189cc7dc9406a7183e899d14a23c032b2c3099d703ae00619ac`\n- VMware ZIP SHA-256: `da4def91a6e4cb427de5c04e53355af9fe4caf394a80087e66609a226ab93cc7`\n\n## Qualified preview tasks\n\nInstall the included original 7-Zip x64 MSI. Open its original file manager, select Documents with a single click, open it and nested folders with a double-click, and use Backspace to return. Real names/details include an independently known file size and unchanged stored bytes. Help/About executes the original menu and dialog procedures; the parent remains disabled until the real OK button closes the dialog. Original move/resize/minimize/maximize/restore/input/close behavior is retained.\n\nCompact, ordinary and actual physical 3840x2160/200% profiles pass. The supported console/MSI installation/archive/extraction/removal/reinstall workflow verifies all 106 original payload hashes on all three profiles. The exact enabled-device VMware ZIP installs, opens/moves/closes the original window and boots twice without the ISO, leaving the existing VM inventory unchanged.\n\nAll **60 native groups and 13 supporting host groups** pass, including the retained runtime/file/settings/fault regressions. The 74-task frozen-candidate campaign and every required canonical/executed observer source are independently checked. New owned dialog/menu/list/input/protection and compact raster lifetimes each repeat 21 times with zero retained pages. Nineteen independent physical-pixel checks pass at compact and actual 4K sizes. Real page-protection tests handle eight hardware access faults per execution, then run the original console again. These owned tests do not substitute for original application tasks.\n\n[Native acceptance](https://github.com/enginsoysal/engacer-os/blob/53c7eaffb8f730eb947270a2d41001a2229feb74/evidence/M14/5/acceptance-results.json), [resource accounting](https://github.com/enginsoysal/engacer-os/blob/53c7eaffb8f730eb947270a2d41001a2229feb74/evidence/M14/5/resources.json), [visual scope](https://github.com/enginsoysal/engacer-os/blob/53c7eaffb8f730eb947270a2d41001a2229feb74/evidence/M14/5/visual-review.json).\n\n## Resource boundaries\n\nFixed desktop session data are **557,676 bytes**, 16 fewer than M14.4: obsolete cursor-owner state and its alignment were removed. Font coverage remains 251,248 bytes. This is component accounting, not total OS RAM or a speed comparison. Original GUI initialization retains one declared shared registered-format cache page; repeated closes add no unexplained pages. The full M14.15 CPU/RAM/storage qualification is still mandatory.\n\nImage records remain 72 bytes. Process image memory is bounded to 16 MiB, with 256 objects and 512 entries per list. Input queues remain one lazily allocated page per used queue. No new periodic compatibility worker is introduced. Read-only/read-write/execute-read protections change real private page-table rights; unsupported modes fail. [Memory profile](https://github.com/enginsoysal/engacer-os/blob/53c7eaffb8f730eb947270a2d41001a2229feb74/docs/architecture/memory-m145.md), [image limits](https://github.com/enginsoysal/engacer-os/blob/53c7eaffb8f730eb947270a2d41001a2229feb74/docs/architecture/image-lists-m145.md).\n\n## Limits and next work\n\nFull GUI archive operations, shared Open/Save dialogs, reusable MSI/EXE installation and complete original-app scenarios remain later gates. Original date text clips at the app-requested column widths; arbitrary header dragging, ellipsis, drag services, live directory notifications and universal control behavior are unqualified. The legacy console notice remains conservative; follow the named preview tasks in the current guide. Network/root labels do not establish network-share support.\n\nBoth mandatory original Notepad++ and SumatraPDF startup diagnostics advance past real VirtualProtect calls and stop at FlsAlloc before an interface. Their required runtimes remain M14.10 work and all complete installer/use/save/restart/removal scenarios remain blocking M14.12 requirements. No target was removed. Firefox is download-only. No universal hardware, GPU gaming, unlimited uptime, general Windows compatibility or faster-than-Windows claim is made.\n\n[Install](https://github.com/enginsoysal/engacer-os/blob/53c7eaffb8f730eb947270a2d41001a2229feb74/docs/handbook/install-m145.md), [first day](https://github.com/enginsoysal/engacer-os/blob/53c7eaffb8f730eb947270a2d41001a2229feb74/docs/handbook/first-day-m145.md), [Windows tasks](https://github.com/enginsoysal/engacer-os/blob/53c7eaffb8f730eb947270a2d41001a2229feb74/docs/handbook/windows-m145.md), [drawing](https://github.com/enginsoysal/engacer-os/blob/53c7eaffb8f730eb947270a2d41001a2229feb74/docs/architecture/drawing-m145.md), [menus](https://github.com/enginsoysal/engacer-os/blob/53c7eaffb8f730eb947270a2d41001a2229feb74/docs/architecture/menus-m145.md), [lists](https://github.com/enginsoysal/engacer-os/blob/53c7eaffb8f730eb947270a2d41001a2229feb74/docs/architecture/lists-m145.md), [stage gates](https://github.com/enginsoysal/engacer-os/blob/53c7eaffb8f730eb947270a2d41001a2229feb74/docs/milestones/m14-5.md), [ordered M14 plan](https://github.com/enginsoysal/engacer-os/blob/53c7eaffb8f730eb947270a2d41001a2229feb74/docs/milestones/m14.md).\n\nUse the matching [VMware ZIP](https://github.com/enginsoysal/engacer-os/releases/download/m145-v0.14.5/EngacerOS-M14STAGE5-VMware.zip), [ISO](https://github.com/enginsoysal/engacer-os/releases/download/m145-v0.14.5/EngacerOS-M14STAGE5.iso) and [checksums](https://github.com/enginsoysal/engacer-os/releases/download/m145-v0.14.5/M14STAGE5-SHA256SUMS.txt).\n"}